00:42:29,338 --> 00:42:31,590
on doing a commentary on a movie - -

671
00:42:31,799 --> 00:42:36,804
Oh , yeah , he 's , like , actually seeing the blood coursing through her veins .

672
00:42:37,012 --> 00:42:41,183
These are all ideas that we hoped to do when we planned it out .

673
00:42:41,392 --> 00:42:45,146
And then , of course , we had to find ways to be able to do this imagery .

674
00:42:45,354 --> 00:42:52,153
But - - And some worked really very , very successfully , and some not at all .

675
00:42:52,361 --> 00:42:56,991
But you can see that it was a production that was full of ideas

676
00:42:57,199 --> 00:43:00,411
and basically innovations

677
00:43:00,619 --> 00:43:03,622
to try to bring this old tale

678
00:43:03,831 --> 00:43:06,375
this beloved , you know , horror classic

679
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:08,502
Stoker 's Dracula - -

680
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:12,298
Once again , to film without just following the path

681
00:43:12,506 --> 00:43:14,300
